# Certificates are obtained automatically from Let's Encrypt when this
# directory holds nothing else. That is the right default for a server with a
# public domain and nothing in front of it.
#
# To override where the certificate comes from, drop another .caddy file in
# here. Its directives land inside the site block, so a Cloudflare Origin CA
# pair is one line:
#
#     tls /etc/caddy/certs/origin.pem /etc/caddy/certs/origin.key
#
# See "Serving over HTTPS" in the README for the cases that need this --
# a proxied Cloudflare record is the common one, because Let's Encrypt's
# HTTP-01 challenge is answered by Cloudflare rather than by this server.
#
# This file is not decoration. With an empty directory Caddy logs
# "No files matching import glob pattern" on every start, which reads as a
# misconfiguration to anyone tailing the logs for the first time.
